<Docs
  title="InfraNode GPTs for ChatGPT: city data in the store"
  description="All InfraNode GPTs in the ChatGPT Store: live data for German cities, real-time public transit, public procurement and station boards, keyless and free right inside ChatGPT."
  current="gpts"
  lang="en"
  altLangPath="/gpts/"
>
  <JsonLd
    slot="jsonld"
    type="ItemList"
    items={gpts.map((g) => ({ name: g.name, url: g.url, description: g.description }))}
  />

  <h1>InfraNode GPTs in the ChatGPT Store</h1>
  <p>
    InfraNode is available as ready-made GPTs in the ChatGPT Store: each GPT
    uses the keyless, free InfraNode API and answers questions about German
    cities with live data, each with source and license. From an all-rounder to
    city-specific live GPTs and specialists for transit departures, public
    procurement and station boards. All are free and usable without sign-up.
  </p>

  <div class="gpt-grid">
    {
      gpts.map((g) => (
        <article class="gpt-card">
          <h2 class="gpt-card__name">{g.name}</h2>
          <p class="gpt-card__desc">{g.description}</p>
          <p class="gpt-card__cta">
            {/* aria-label with the GPT name: distinguishable link names instead
                of 8x identical "Open in ChatGPT" (WCAG 2.4.4). */}
            <a
              href={g.url}
              rel="noopener"
              target="_blank"
              aria-label={`${g.name}: Open in ChatGPT (opens in a new window)`}
            >
              <strong>Open in ChatGPT</strong>
            </a>
          </p>
          <p class="gpt-card__label">Example prompts:</p>
          <ul class="gpt-card__prompts">
            {g.prompts.map((p) => (
              <li>{p}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <p>
      InfraNode is an independent open data project and is not affiliated with
      the cities, transit authorities, Deutsche Bahn or OpenAI mentioned here.
      All data comes from official open data sources and is delivered with
      origin and license.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Prefer to build your own?</h2>
  <p>
    You can also build your own GPT with the InfraNode API. The
    <a href="/en/chatgpt/">ChatGPT and GPT actions page</a> shows how with the
    curated GPT action. For MCP-capable clients such as Claude there is also the
    <a href="/en/mcp/">InfraNode MCP server</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>

